  "season": {
    "eyebrow": "By season",
    "heading": "Three ways to read the year.",
    "cols": [
      {
        "kicker": "Chase the sun",
        "heading": "When home turns grey",
        "body": "Through the Indian winter, and again in the monsoon, the answer is somewhere warm and dry: the Maldives and Seychelles, the Southern-hemisphere summer of South Africa, Australia and New Zealand, the steady Gulf. We book the festive and New-Year peaks early. The best water villas and suites go first."
      },
      {
        "kicker": "Chase the snow",
        "heading": "When you want winter",
        "body": "December to March is the Alps, Hokkaido and the high north: Switzerland, France, Japan, the aurora latitudes. It overlaps the Christmas–New-Year break and the long weekends of the new year. That is exactly why the planning starts months ahead, not weeks."
      },
      {
        "kicker": "Chase the value",
        "heading": "The shoulder seasons",
        "body": "The quiet art is the in-between: late April–June and September–October, when Europe and the Mediterranean are warm but emptied, fares ease, and the famous places feel like yours. The shoulder rewards anyone who can travel a week either side of the crowd. We plan for it."
      }
    ]
  },
  "calendar": {
    "eyebrow": "Your calendar",
    "heading": "The dates that shape the year.",
    "lede": "When the country travels at once, prices rise and seats vanish. Knowing the windows is half the planning.",
    "items": [
      {
        "tag": "Oct–Nov · Diwali",
        "body": "The festival of lights falls in the autumn: a natural break, and a peak. Demand on long-haul and the nearer escapes climbs sharply. We hold flights and stays well ahead, because the good fares are gone weeks before the dates."
      },
      {
        "tag": "Dec–Jan · Winter break",
        "body": "Christmas through New Year is the single busiest stretch of the travel year. Alpine snow, the Southern summer and the Gulf all peak together; this is the window to plan furthest in advance: six months is not too early."
      },
      {
        "tag": "May–Jun · Summer holidays",
        "body": "The long school break is when families travel. Europe, the longer journeys and the cooler escapes fill fast. A June trip to Europe means the Schengen file opens in March. The lead time is the whole game."
      },
      {
        "tag": "The long weekends",
        "body": "Scattered through the year: Republic Day, Holi, the August cluster, and others, each is a chance at a short, nearer journey. They reward booking early and choosing places within a comfortable flight: the Gulf, Sri Lanka, Thailand, Singapore."
      }
    ]
  },
